# DOC_CANON — {PROJECT_NAME}

The project's **running documentation canon** — the cumulative, locked record of what each closed WP
delivered. It is built forward (never retroactively): at every **CLOSE gate**, the closing WP's LOD500 is
distilled into a one-line entry appended below. This is the L26 **DOC-close obligation**: a WP cannot reach
CLOSE until this file reflects its LOD500 (P9 — no after-the-fact documentation). The Ambassador
(`core.modules.management.governance_audit`) audits this across spokes; the builder/architect writes it.

Detector: `validate_aos` **Check 59** (`python3 -m core.modules.management.doc_canon --check`) — advisory in a
standalone `validate_aos .` run, **HARD at the CLOSE gate / in cold-integration CI** (`AOS_DOC_CLOSE_GATE=1`;
with `AOS_DOC_WP=<wp_id>` the closing WP must appear below). This project holds its own
`_aos/context/DOC_CANON.md` (propagated structure, project-local entries). This file was bootstrapped from
the lean-kit template `DOC_CANON.md.template`; replace every `{…}` placeholder before first use.

## Structure
Each locked entry is a single bullet under **Locked LOD500 entries**, newest last:
`- <WP_ID> — <YYYY-MM-DD> — <one-line: what shipped + the decisive gate that locked it>`.
Group by milestone with a `### <milestone>` sub-header. No prose beyond the one-liner — depth lives in the
WP's own `SPEC_LOD*` + gate verdicts. The four sections below (Structure / Quality / Procedure / Locked LOD500
entries) are required and are what Check 59 validates for well-formedness.

## Quality
- One line per WP, factual, present-tense; name the artifact and the gate that locked it (e.g. "VALIDATE
  cross-engine PASS").
- Cite governance with qualified references (`[<project-label> _aos/context/CODE_STANDARDS.md CS-N]`, ADR ids).
- Never edit a locked entry's meaning after the fact; corrections are appended, not rewritten.
- Keep it scannable: a reader should reconstruct *what the project is now* from this file alone.

## Procedure (DOC-close obligation · L26)
1. At a WP's **CLOSE** gate (HG-2 / team_00), distill its LOD500 into one entry and append it below.
2. Run `AOS_DOC_CLOSE_GATE=1 AOS_DOC_WP=<wp_id> bash …/validate_aos.sh .` — Check 59 must be **0 FAIL**
   (it blocks CLOSE if `<wp_id>` is not yet reflected here).
3. Commit the DOC_CANON update **with** the LOD500 lock (same CLOSE commit), then flip metadata → `LOD500_LOCKED`.
4. Standalone `validate_aos .` stays advisory (0 FAIL) so clones/CI of in-flight branches are never blocked.

> **Backfill note (LOD_STANDARD_v5 §5.6).** A backfilled LOD500 (as-built for code that shipped before its
> LOD ladder existed) is distilled into exactly one entry here, the same as a build-time LOD500. Author the
> backfill LOD500 with the `ASBUILT_LOD500_AUTHORING_RUNBOOK_v5` runbook — **no retro LOD300/400 is created**.

